# Specialist agent output folders (CLAUDE 1 / CLAUDE 2 / CLAUDE 4).
#
# Reference material to be inspected, compared and SELECTIVELY integrated into
# the canonical backend — not a second copy of the application. Each contains its
# own backend/ mirror, and committing them would put three competing
# rule_engine.py / ocr_extraction.py / schema.py files in the repository, which is
# precisely the duplication the architecture forbids: one canonical
# implementation per responsibility. CLAUDE 2 alone is 32M.
#
# They are deliberately NOT deleted — verified work still has to be lifted out of
# them. Anything genuinely additive gets adapted into backend/ or frontend/ with a
# note in IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md recording where it came from.
CLAUDE 1/
CLAUDE 2/
CLAUDE 4/
